* AC analysis on an MNA circuit: series RLC, output across C1.
*
*   V1 in 0 DC 0 AC 1
*   L1 in n2 1e-3      1 mH
*   R1 n2 out 1m       1 mOhm
*   C1 out 0 1n        1 nF
*
* Node `in` has NO self-term in its KCL row (i(V1) + i(L1) = 0): the case that
* needs a pivot-safe ordering in the small-signal matrix.
*
* Closed form: H(s) = V(out)/V(in) = 1 / (1 + sRC + s^2 LC)
*   f0 = 1/(2*pi*sqrt(LC)) = 159.155 kHz      <- the peak
*   Q  = sqrt(L/C)/R       = 1e6             <- 120 dB, but see below
*   |H| = 1 (0 dB) again at sqrt(2)*f0 = 225.1 kHz, then it falls as 1/f^2
*   (-40 dB/decade: +4.86 dB at 199.5 kHz, -31.7 dB at 1 MHz).
*
* The bandwidth is f0/Q = 0.159 Hz, while DEC 100/decade steps 3.7 kHz at f0, so
* the sweep CANNOT resolve the peak: 119.8 is the grid point nearest f0, not
* the true Q. Every simulator shows the same sampled peak for this sweep —
* refine the sweep (LIN, or a few thousand points) to see the real one.


V1 in 0 DC 0 AC 1
L1 in n2 1e-3
R1 n2 out 1m
C1 out 0 1n
.AC DEC 100 100 1meg
.END